PK␀␀␀␀␀␀␀!␀QÒp­%␀␀­%␀␀ø␀␀␀f020-even-leading-odd-tail-public-20261021_v1/accepted-history/history-c86929554da6cba6/f020-single-leading-digit-comparison/dependencies/accepted-theorem/dependencies/leading-two/dependencies/even-low-digit/exploratory-review/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md# Independent audit: the even-degree low-digit family

20 October 2026 UTC. Local audit only; no external mutation. This review concerns the original H/P polynomials, ordinary derivatives, and algebraic-square kernels. Final candidate byte binding is recorded separately in VERDICT.json.

## Scope reviewed

For every odd prime p, r>=2, s>r, primitive characteristic-zero p^s-th root q, and odd low digit d=2c+1<p, put N=p^r and n=N+d. The reviewed claim is all-root squarefreeness of both original polynomials and nonvanishing of the original ordinary-square diagonal kernel at every P_n root. The proof also gives its stated outer-root count and root-dependent derivative valuations.

This includes the originally requested n=N+1 family. It does not claim arbitrary degree, arbitrary intermediate digits, arbitrary leading digits, arbitrary odd-composite order, a new all-root discriminant formula, or global F020/F023 closure.

## 1. The abandoned central two-term inference is false

The independent exact cyclotomic computation reconstructs the original H recurrence and translates at geometric centers. For p=3,r=2,s=3, its central even Newton hull is (0,15),(4,6),(10,0), giving four roots of valuation 9/4, not two roots of valuation 3/2. For p=3,r=4,s=5, the central slope is 81/10, while the first slopes at centers a=1 and a=3 are 80/9 and 26/3. These are all below the old radius beta=9 and above the enlarged radius alpha=8.

Thus neither the guessed p/2 slope nor reuse of the old closed beta disks is valid. The candidate does not use either inference. The complete recorded coefficient valuations and residual units, including all Newton faces rather than selected terms, are retained in CENTER_HULLS.json.

## 2. The cap modification is exact

For even r=2h, alpha=p^h-1 lies strictly between p^(h-1) and p^h. Therefore the truncated valuation sum is exactly

    T(m)=T_h(m)-floor(m/p^h),
    R(m)=R_h(m)+floor(m/p^h).

The highest residue-class increment remains positive. The consecutive-string proof consequently gives the strict upper bound alpha+T(l-1), including l=1. The proof uses a maximizing distance; this is what justifies equality with the minimum even when the two compared valuations coincide. Centers modulo beta suffice because their differences have valuation at least beta>=alpha.

For odd r the original cap beta and original T_h,R_h remain in use; the even-r cap change is not applied there.

## 3. The strengthened digit bound is uniform

The source digit proof pays for each added digit contribution p^(a-h), a>=h, from the available slack

    (2h-a)(p-1)p^(a-1)/2.

The required inequality reduces to

    (2h-a)(p-1)p^(h-1)>=2.

It holds for all a<=2h-1. In the smallest case p=3,h=1,a=1 it is equality, not a strict inequality. This is harmless: strictness for every positive even m comes from the separate positive term W(floor(sum(d_a)/2)), since the digit sum is then positive and even. This distinction is necessary and is present in the proof.

The complement identity continues to hold after adding floor(m/beta), because N is divisible by beta. The exact resulting margins are beta for even r and ((p-1)/2)p^(r-1) for odd r. They are at least alpha. Since an uncovered root has d0<alpha, the final margin is strictly positive even when the displayed non-strict bound is sharp.

## 4. Full ordinary derivative control on the enlarged disks

The ordinary geometric-Newton derivative double sum is complete. Its three exhaustive cases are m=0, positive even m, and odd m. The same strengthened R bound proves that the unique maximal bracket remains (k,m)=(p^2,0), of value B+p. No differentiation of a characteristic-p repeated factor is used. The surviving factor z^(p^2-1) has residual 1.

For the neighboring even polynomial H_(N-1), the k=0 term must be retained. It is the unique minimum of valuation B, because every positive even k has strict digit slack. The ordinary derivative bound follows from both parity cases of m, with j=k-m. In the odd-m case, j<N, so ord_p((N-j)/2)=ord_p(j) is justified.

The original H/P coordinate change has unit ordinary coordinate derivatives near the relevant roots. For the whole-disk P_N derivative assertion, the differentiated prefactor contributes valuation at least v(N)=r v(p)>D. This uses actual ramification v(p)=phi(p^s), not a characteristic-p truncation. Thus the reviewed whole-disk statements concern P_N' and P_(N-1), not P_n' away from its roots.

## 5. Odd shifted tails and all-root partition

For d=2c+1<p, the coefficient of X in A_d has exact weight c because the corresponding Hermite coefficient is (-1)^c(2c+1)!! and is nonzero modulo p. The even tail B_d has a nonzero constant matching product of weight c. All higher terms are strictly larger at x=v(X)>1/2.

Writing A_d=X U(X^2) and B_d=V(X^2) proves v(C_d)=-x. In the logarithmic derivative, the two composed-polynomial logarithmic derivatives have weight at least x-1, which is strictly greater than -x. The -1/X term therefore uniquely dominates, proving the exact ordinary derivative valuation v(C_d')=-2x. This remains valid for c=0, when the two logarithmic derivatives are zero.

The outer Hermite reduction is Y^N He_d. Only its 2c nonzero simple roots are lifted as simple roots. The remaining factor has degree N+1 and is kept with multiplicity until the later all-root proof. Zero is explicitly excluded in the original P_n by its nonzero constant matching product. Thus division by A_d is legitimate at every inner root.

## 6. The covering proof includes every perturbation term

At an inner root, the P/H coordinate factors are units and v(z+1)=x>1/2; in particular z is a unit. The relative perturbation weight is N-x. For k=N-1-2u, 0<=u<=A, exact reflection gives

    W(N-1)-W(k)=W(2u).

The remaining Newton string has length 2u+1. Its strict bound gives the candidate's ratio lower bound

    N-x-alpha-W(u)+R(2u).

This includes u=0, the k=N-1 term, and u=A, the constant k=0 term. The complement identity and superadditivity give W(u)-R(2u)<=B-R(N-1), so each perturbing term is strictly above H_N by more than C-x>0. The argument does not assume simplicity, does not discard a split cluster, and does not rely on an unproved residual factorization.

## 7. Root-dependent separation and original kernels

After differentiating before root evaluation, the first bracketed term has exact valuation D. The perturbation has exact valuation N+B-2x: its C_d'P_(N-1) part is strictly below its C_d P_(N-1)' part, because x>0. Equality of the two main valuations would require x=p/2.

The complete covering excludes that value. On the central disk x>=alpha>=p-1>p/2. On any other disk x=p^ord_p(a), since the center valuation is at most beta/p<alpha. Such an x is either 1 or at least p. Therefore the original ordinary derivative valuation is exactly

    c+x+min(D,N+B-2x),

and is finite. The H/P unit coordinate factors transfer this result to H_n. No root meets the ramification points X=+/-2, because every P_n root has positive valuation.

Every recurrence edge below n is nonzero. Consecutive P polynomials are coprime by backwards recurrence. The original algebraic-square Christoffel-Darboux identity therefore gives a nonzero diagonal kernel at every root. This is not a positivity or absolute-value-square argument. Algebraic nonvanishing is preserved by every characteristic-zero embedding.

## 8. Independent exact controls and limitations

The audit scripts import no author checker. They include:

- Complete all-term integer checks for 12 modest (p,r) grids, and separately labelled large-r random controls up to r=31. These test digit strictness, complementation, both covering endpoints, the full ordinary base derivative double sum, and the full neighboring derivative double sum.
- 26 exact actual-field disk certificates for H_N and H_(N-1), including p=3,r=4,s=5 where D exceeds phi(p^s). Polynomials are reconstructed in Z[q]/Phi_(p^s), translated exactly, and converted from q to t=q-1. The distinct residue classes of j+phi(p^s)ord_p(c_j) make the computed minimum exact. All constant units match independent products of the exact factor units, using p/t^phi -> -1.
- Complete even H Newton faces at 13 central and noncentral translations.
- Exact rational H/P, ordinary-square CD, shifted-tail, and cleared root-dependent derivative-elimination identities.
- 19 finite-field nonzero-resultant controls for both original H and P, with verified primitive q of order p^s. These include every odd d<p in the selected cases and an additional s>r+1 control.

Finite computations are falsification/transcription controls, not the proof of the unlimited theorem. The uniform conclusion rests on the arguments reviewed above.

## 9. Independence disclosure

This reviewer proposed an unused alternative gamma-radius reflection simplification while the author was developing the enlarged-disk route. It is not used in the candidate. The reviewer independently checked the alpha route after the author supplied it, and requested explicit unit-coordinate accounting, but supplied no essential lemma for that route.

The reviewer also suggested the optional odd-tail extension shortly before receiving the expanded draft. The author reports that the full expanded proof had already been written before that suggestion arrived, and that the suggestion was not used. The overlap is disclosed rather than hidden. This is an independent mathematical audit with iterative adversarial communication, not a claim that the reviewer had no contact with the author. A separate fresh frozen-byte challenge remains appropriate for final independent acceptance.
