## Frozen target and verdict

**ACCEPTED WITHIN THE EXACT STATED SCOPE.** The complete uniform second-layer theorem, its original derivative units, and the qualified combined r=2 conclusion are accepted.

The exact target manifest is 736177befd117445980e7a29adb2582fdaf701fbd247e32c7b9f4cf460664aaa. No author or accepted-source file was edited, no external write was performed, and no essential mathematical repair was supplied by this reviewer. The proof was reconstructed independently before final freezing, then checked against the exact frozen report. All frozen-source and replay gates below passed.

## Scope and normalization

The new result concerns the original recurrence P_(j+1)=X P_j-(1-q^j)P_(j-1), degree n=cpÂ²+1, even 2<=c<p, p>=5, all s>2, and those pairs with p dividing A_c=R_c(-1). Put N=pÂ², B=p(p-1), d=B/2, K=c(N+2B)/2, XÂ²=t^p U, and P_n/X=t^K f(U), with t=q-1 and v(t)=1. The result is v(U+1)>1 and v(f_U)=d+1, with normalized unit R_c'(-1)/8, at every exceptional root. The original P derivative has value K+d+1 and unit -R_c'(-1)/4. These are distinct normalized derivatives, not conflicting statements.

Combined with the exactly bound accepted general criterion, all even 2<=c<p adjacent r=2 families are squarefree and have nonzero original algebraic-square Christoffel-Darboux kernel. The p=3,c=2 boundary is inherited solely from the accepted exact P_19 theorem; its exceptional P derivative value is 76/3, not the new first-order formula. No arbitrary-degree, arbitrary-digit, odd-c, composite-order, global F020/F023, FFT, cost, or historical-novelty assertion is accepted.

## Dependency qualification

The accepted general author manifest is e19104be98018ea10de85dd648b3b2634664150ea24994300e28ac56fe889ec7; its final independent-review manifest is a7990e625de81f3797ac13bbad7d7c817eb65aee195e5690f84de6ca7540c3c7. That dependency supplies the unconditional disk geometry, exact zero, ordinary coefficientwise derivative bound, neighbor values at the residual root locus, and simplicity away from the exceptional locus. It does not prove exceptional nonsimplicity or exceptional simplicity. The new proof genuinely supplies the missing lift.

The c=2 public archive has SHA-256 667b37740cd2229082899e726a6efdb7e2be8b2e5d177eed5d3869bbcb79ec4e. Its acceptance binds author manifest 072e4134daea3f759d79550c891027abb0410ed38aac6826635fee085f730147 and fresh-review manifest b7583a6324271df5defc71514c871562a88c62cfb69ed736b62d3814abebff47. Its p=3 theorem is qualified as inherited work. The copied c8 comparison report has SHA-256 a916d0137814f8013cca6375cfa3b70967cc9501eb4bb29adb3cb142b4e53477 and is only a normalization comparison, not a premise proving a family from fixed jets.

## Independent mathematical reconstruction

### 1. Geometry, coefficientwise bounds, and the derivative being studied

The p disjoint X disks each contain cp roots of F=P_n/X, counted with multiplicity, exhausting degree cpÂ². The central disk has v(X)=p/2; every noncentral disk has v(X)=1. Zero is an additional simple exact P_n root. On the central disk the exact ordinary chain rule is F'(mu Y)=2t^K mu^(-1)Y f_U(YÂ²), muÂ²=t^p. Therefore the accepted coefficientwise bound v_G(F')>=D yields v_G(f_U)>=D-K+p/2=d. This retains every characteristic-zero integer derivative factor, including multiples of p.

The residual is R_c(U)^p. The Hermite recurrence and M_c'=cM_(c-1) prove separability of M_c modulo p for p>c; its constant term is a unit. Thus R_c is separable, and A_c=0 implies R_c'(-1) is a unit. Exactly two residual Y roots YÂ²=-1 occur, each with multiplicity p. Hence exactly 2p X roots are affected, before simplicity is established. The neighbor M=P_(cN-1) has exact value E at this residual root locus, not necessarily at every central boundary point. The draft correctly restricts division by M accordingly.

### 2. Uniform slack and all nonpivot terms

On the central boundary, N_m has exact value T(m)=m+(p/2-1)ceil(m/p). For m=lN+ap+b, 0<=a,b<p, direct subtraction gives

    2(T(m)-W(m)/2)=a(p-1)+b+(p-2)1_(b>0).

Thus zero slack occurs exactly at multiples of N and every nonzero slack is at least g=(p-1)/2>1. This identity is valid for every allowed c, including c=p-1, rather than being inferred from a finite enumeration.

For H_(cN-1), the odd pivots k=lN attain E; every other term has value at least E+g. The derivative expansion is the ordinary Newton derivative identity. Its termwise bound is E+W(j)/2-p^ord_p(j)+Delta(m). Only j=1,p can produce the deficit -1/2. If m is not a multiple of N, Delta(m) resolves it; if it is, the parity and N-level floor deficit supply B/2. This proves the full M' coefficientwise bound >=E, including all possible borderline terms.

For H_(cN)', the excess above D is bounded below by p+W(j-1)/2-p^ord_p(j)+Delta(m). The cases ord_p(j)=0,1 give respectively >=p-1 and >=g; ord_p(j)=2 has zero minimum only at j=N, with every higher multiple at least W/2 above that minimum. At j=N, parity leaves precisely m=lN for odd 1<=l<c. These are all pivots. Every other derivative term is >=D+g, so none reaches the first correction D+1.

For H_(cN), the pivots are k=jN with j even. At every nonpivot, the N-level floor deficit is at least B and Delta(k)>=g. The total gap is at least B/2+g=(pÂ²-1)/2>p. This justifies discarding all nonpivots in the deeper root-location calculation, not merely the leading residual calculation.

### 3. Characteristic-p cancellation and every leading-digit pivot

The grouped product identity product_(a=0)^(p-1)(Z+A(1+h)^a)-(Z+A)^p divisible by h^(p-1) follows from the Gaussian binomial coefficients, whose interior h orders are p-1. With h=t^p, grouping N_N into p-factor blocks gives relative error at least p(p-2)/2 in the zero-residue group and p(p-2) otherwise. Both exceed p for p>=5.

Consequently N_N=N_p^p(1+error>p). The odd-edge product C0=w_(2N)/Q_N similarly satisfies C0=-t^N D0^(2p)(1+error>p). The p-divisible group is an exact Frobenius identity; the other groups have the stated error. Both R0/t^(p-1) and D0/t^(p-1) have expansion -(1+t/2+O(tÂ²)). Together with SÂ²=zXÂ²=-zt^p and z=-1+error of value p/2, this proves v(N_NÂ²+C0)>W+p at XÂ²=-t^p. No residual-root lifting assumption enters this scalar identity.

For factorial blocks, each internal edge shift by a multiple of N changes the edge by order at least N, while the original internal edge has order at most p. Thus the relative error is at least B. Endpoint ratios are h+O(t^N), with h<p a unit. This proves w_(hN)=h!w_N^h(1+error>=B) and Q_(hN)=h!Q_N^h(1+error>=B) in the needed ranges. The corresponding Newton-product shift has relative error >=N-p/2>p.

For each even j with u=(c-j)/2, the pivot becomes c! C0^u N_N^j/(j!2^u u!), modulo absolute value >K+p. Replacing N_NÂ² by -C0 with its proven relative error and summing gives C0^(c/2) A_c. This is a genuine all-c identity; it is not a fit to finitely many exceptional primes. Since A_c=0 in characteristic p, the sum has order >K+p. The quotient perturbation a_(cN)M/X has value at least K+d>K+p and cannot alter that conclusion.

### 4. The mixed-characteristic transfer remains valid even when K>e

The original even quotient has integer coefficients in t and XÂ². A coefficient of X^(2l) contains m-l recurrence edges, where m=cN/2. After XÂ²=-t^p, every integer monomial therefore has t degree at least m+(p-1)l>=m. The characteristic-p computation shows every coefficient through degree K+p is divisible by p. At the actual primitive q, every such monomial has value at least e+m, and

    e+m-K >= (p-c)B >= B > p.

All unit-coefficient terms start above K+p. Thus v(f(-1))>p holds for every s>2 and every primitive phase. This proves the all-s claim without the false requirement e>K+p. The mixed-characteristic coefficient lattice is essential and is explicitly present.

After U=-1+V, h(V)=sum a_jV^j remains integral coefficientwise and its ordinary derivative remains >=d. The coefficient a_p is a unit; for 1<=j<p, v(a_j)>=d since j is a p-adic unit. If any affected root had 0<v(V)<=1, the a_pV^p term would be uniquely smallest: below the constant by the just-proved bound, below every lower-degree term since d>p, and below every higher-degree term by integrality. This contradiction proves v(V)>1 at every affected root, including both signs and every multiplicity-p branch.

### 5. The first nonzero original derivative layer

The exact ratio of the l-th H_(cN)' pivot to the paired H_(cN-1) pivot is a_(cN)z^(N-1)Q_(uN+A)/(Q_(uN)a_N). The shifted Q ratio is Q_A(1+error>=B), uniformly in u. Because all nonpivot gaps are g>1, the entire paired sums have the same scalar ratio through relative order one. At the affected locus, M has exact value E, so cancellation cannot invalidate the error bound or the division.

The original coordinate prefactor derivative contributes at least 2e+K>D+1. The remaining coordinate factor is 2z^N/(z-1)=1+error>1. The actual mixed-characteristic edge a_N/(-t^N) is also 1+error>1. The normalized Q_A factor is

    Q_A/(-t^B)=1-t/8+error>1.

This follows directly from the p-unit edge expansions: the first-order sum over p-nondivisible indices is (pÂ²-1)/8=-1/8 modulo p, and p-divisible indices have no first-order term. All removed p-multiples have value >1 after normalization.

Thus XÂ²P_(cN)'/(a_(cN)M)=U(1-t/8)+error>1. In the exact ordinary identity F'=P_(cN)'-a_(cN)M'/X+a_(cN)M/XÂ², the middle term is relatively higher by at least p/2>1. Since U=-1+error>1, the full bracket is t/8+error>1. Therefore v(F')=D+1, without differentiating any inseparable residual.

The scalar converting this bracket to f_U has value d and residue (-c epsilon/2)M_(c-1)(Y^p)/YÂ³. At either YÂ²=-1, Y^p=epsilon Y and M_c'=cM_(c-1)=2Y R_c'(-1); the residue simplifies to R_c'(-1). Hence f_U/t^(d+1) has unit R_c'(-1)/8, nonzero automatically. At an F root, P_n'=2U t^K f_U gives the unit -R_c'(-1)/4. The H multiplier is (-1)^(c/2), so H and P valuations coincide but their units need not.

For c8,p11, R'_8(-1)=80=3 modulo 11 gives f_U unit 10 and original P unit 2. These exactly reconcile the accepted fixed-case report, rather than silently switching normalizations.

### 6. Completion of the original objects

The complete count is one exact zero, cp(p-1) noncentral roots, (c-2)p regular central roots when exceptional, and 2p lifted roots. The total is cpÂ²+1. Their derivative values are respectively K, D+1, K+d, K+d+1. In the nonexceptional case all cp central roots have value K+d. No disk is omitted.

The original H/P coordinate maps are unramified at these roots: P roots reduce to zero and are not +/-2, while H roots reduce to -1 and are nonzero. At a root the derivative of the prefactor vanishes exactly, so squarefreeness and derivative valuations transfer. Every recurrence edge below n is nonzero; backward recurrence excludes a common root of P_n and P_(n-1). The original diagonal Christoffel-Darboux identity therefore has nonzero right side P_n'P_(n-1)/w_(n-1) at every P_n root. The squares are algebraic, not absolute-value squares. Injectivity and Galois conjugacy transfer the conclusion to every characteristic-zero primitive embedding.

## Independent exact controls and replay

The independent implementation does not import author or dependency checker code. It follows the original one-step P recurrence in the complete cyclic q algebra over Z/pÂ², carries ordinary U-derivative jets at U=-1, reduces to the canonical cyclotomic basis, and performs the exact q=1+t conversion. Canonical weights j+e*v_p(coefficient) are distinct below precision 2e; the unit p/t^e=-1 is retained. Accumulation bounds are checked before int64 arithmetic. Nothing uses floating-point evaluation.

Fourteen actual cases cover c2,p5/7; c8,p11; c10,p19; prime-boundary c16,p17; and negative nonexceptional c4,p5, c4/c6,p7, c8,p13. Phases include 1, 2, and -1, plus p5,s4. All exceptional constant values exceed K+p and all tested ordinary derivative values and units match K+d+1 and R'_c(-1)/8. The c16,p17 case has K>e and explicitly tests the mixed-characteristic layer.

Every H, neighboring H, ordinary H', and ordinary neighboring H' summand is independently enumerated for seven bounded structural fixtures. The complete pivot sets match, with all nonpivot gaps at least those proved uniformly. Additional controls verify grouped-product divisibility and the normalized Q_A constant/linear terms for p5,7,11. Negative gates retain p3's gap exactly one, the distinct c8 derivative units, omission of half the exceptional roots by keeping one Y disk, the inseparable-residual derivative trap, and the false e>K+p shortcut.

The exact copied author cold replay passed in 1.561 seconds; its regenerated result hash is 93d1130ba84fa5de64da811b085aec3a5a7b828a7edd13217b4ee0eac74826c1. It used an outer 240 CPU-second/300 wall-second cap with 1 GiB address space and 64 MiB file output, and the author's isolated inner controls were capped at 180 CPU seconds/240 wall seconds. Both original and copied author inventories were unchanged.

The final independent clean replay passed byte-for-byte in 15.171 seconds. It was capped at 120 CPU seconds, 180 wall seconds, 1 GiB address space, 32 MiB file output, and one numerical thread. The final exact independent-result hash is e832ab944a2a3e4038ebe065262e194dbd1c89746c83878fb2b6b785e231a5e2.

Seven disposable-copy inventory tests rejected an altered report, the same corruption under Python -O, a missing checker, an extra file, a mismatched seal, a fully rehashed substitute under the wrong external manifest anchor, and a symlink member with otherwise identical bytes. The independent verifier uses explicit checks that remain active under optimization. Full general-author/general-review inventories, the c2 public archive and its p3 acceptance linkage, and the c8 comparison acceptance bytes were independently verified. No source was changed.

These are bounded falsification and transcription checks. The unlimited theorem is proved by the uniform inequalities and identities above, not by the list of cases. No unexpected mathematical control failure occurred and no essential correction was supplied.
